{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Now the man Moses was exceedingly humble.</b> The word ענו is written with a missing י״ו (yod), and he was perfect in the trait of humility; but because he fell short a letter of yod in honoring the Holy Name, blessed be He, in the matter of the Rock, when he said (Numbers 20:10) ״המן הסלע הזה נוציא לכם מים״ — and he should have said יוציא, attributing it to the Holy Name, blessed be He — therefore Scripture omitted that letter in his praise, measure for measure. Thus I have heard, and it is fitting, except that the word occurs in its normal form without deficiency elsewhere. And the addition of מאד ('exceedingly'): for the straight path a person should choose for himself in all other traits is the mean, but in this trait it is proper to incline from the mean and to distance oneself toward the furthest extreme; and from this the Sages, of blessed memory, said: מאד מאד הוי שפל רוח — 'be very, very lowly of spirit.' And the addition of אשר על פני האדמה ('who are upon the face of the earth'), is so that you not understand it except of the lower beings. And understand this, for it is like the matter of (Genesis 6:6) ״וינחם ה׳ כי עשה את האדם בארץ״ — He added בארץ for an intended meaning, and did not say באדמה, because the word ארץ is comprehensive; but when He came to say 'I will blot out,' He specified and said (ibid.) ״מעל פני האדמה״, and there I wrote in its place. And this is what is written (Psalms 145:12) ״להודיע לבני האדם גבורותיו״, and you should understand the expression גבורותיו and His kingship, and this is clear."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:49.642661818Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}